# Production build-time config. COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# The Clerk publishable key is not a secret — it ships inside the browser bundle
# on every page load, which is why Clerk calls it "publishable". The secret key
# (sk_…) is a different thing entirely and must never appear in this repo.
#
# Why it lives here rather than in Dokploy's Environment section:
# Astro bakes PUBLIC_ vars in at BUILD time, and site/Dockerfile consumes this
# one as a Docker `ARG`. A runtime environment variable therefore arrives after
# the static site has already been compiled and has no effect — the build
# silently keeps whatever key it had. That failure is invisible: the site builds,
# deploys and serves normally, just pointed at the wrong Clerk instance. It cost
# a cutover on 2026-08-11, where the site stayed on the development instance
# while the backend had already moved to production, breaking /app/token with a
# 401 (dev-issued session token verified against the production secret).
#
# Committing it makes the production build self-contained: nothing to remember
# in a panel, and the value is version-controlled and reviewable.
#
# Vite/Astro precedence: .env.production overrides .env for production-mode
# builds, so `npm run dev` still picks up the development key from site/.env
# while `npm run build` (and the Docker build) uses this one.
#
# See changes/006-LICENSING-CLERK/006.04-CLERK-PRODUCTION-MIGRATION.md
PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_Y2xlcmsuc2hhZHlub3Rlcy5hcHAk

# Tell Clerk the site hosts its OWN sign-in/sign-up pages. These existed only in
# the gitignored site/.env, so every production build shipped without them and
# Clerk fell back to its hosted Account Portal:
#
#   sign_in_url       https://accounts.shadynotes.app/sign-in
#   after_sign_in_url https://shadynotes.app          <- the homepage
#
# That breaks the desktop app's sign-in whenever the user is NOT already signed
# in. /app/connect sends them to sign in with ?redirect_url=/app/connect?state=…,
# the portal round-trip discards it, and they land on the homepage instead of
# back on the connect page — so the app token is never minted, the
# shadynotes://auth deep link never fires, and the app sits on "Signing in…"
# forever (it has no timeout). Signing in first made it work, which is exactly
# the reported behaviour.
PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up
